{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea","id":1028953,"title":"Crazy Idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-09T03:56:46-08:00","id":1028953,"title":"Crazy Idea","content":"There's a war going.<br /> <br /> You hire a bunch of human gangers/mercs, give them a cannon, charged with cold iron shrapnel and ask them to fire it into the charging army of changelings. Sidhe, for example.<br /> <br /> What happens next? <br /> <br /> My guess, it should be super-deadly, especially if you got more than one.<br /> <br /> But political implications, as well as military, is another matter entirely. And magical implication, too. I'm not even sure, that Dreaming would not simply freak out, like when that Crowbar Incident happened.<br /> <br /> Discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T06:33:20-08:00","id":1029013,"title":"","content":"If I were the ST, the changeling in question would suffer a serious Banality trigger \u2014 probably a dot of Banality for every changeling that dies from the cold iron cannon. Depending on the circumstances, the changeling's faerie soul might even break and s/he'd become a dauntain. I don't think there'd be quite as dramatic a result as trying to bring cold iron into the Dreaming, but if enough changelings die from cold iron at once, the battlefield would almost certainly bear metaphysical scars from the conflict. If there are truly massive casualties, I'd raise the ambient Banality of the area to make it dangerous for Kithain to spend much time there. I'd also borrow a bit from DA: Darkening Sky's Friar's Cross and make Unleashing no longer work there.<br /> <br /> As far as political implications go, the changeling would almost certainly find her/himself hunted by both the Seelie and Unseelie Courts. The Thallain might offer the changeling sanctuary, but they'd have their own agenda. If s/he accepts, the changeling would become their pawn.<br /> <br /> Militarily, the changeling in question might win the battle, but in doing so, s/he would hand a much greater victory to the enemy of all fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 01-09-2017, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:04:42-08:00","id":1029030,"title":"","content":"I'm interest, whether inidirect murder will actually bear any consequences for changeling, as direct does. If changeling officers suffer Banality loss from every death, that happened under their command, that would mean there can be no changeling generals afterwards, as war means a deaths, even with such license as chimerical death. <br /> <br /> I imagine, considering weigth of the crime, sufficiently morivated anti-hero or Shadow Court themselves can do that, knowingly.<br /> <br /> Would someone repeat and implement such weaponry? Or maybe it'll be assembled and clanked loudly, but never used, like nuclear weapons? Heavily supervised (much more, than normally)?<br /> <br /> I always wondered, why nockers didn't use something like that against Sidhe?.. Even after factoring in for magic, they fought on home terrain with knowledge Sidhe didn't have access to.<br /> <br /> Could weaponry like that used in any of the future wars of Concordia? Despite fear and taboo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:45:08-08:00","id":1029058,"title":"","content":"Changeling: The Dreaming has several different kinds of death, some of them are more permanent than others.<br /> <br /> Death by cold iron isn't just murder. It's the annihilation of a piece of the Dreaming. A changeling might be able to justify or rationalize it in their own mind, such as ending a Lost One or a Dauntain, but no matter the reason, it is always the destruction of a piece of the Dreaming and a victory for Banality. Just because the changeling didn't physically light the fuse, doesn't mean they didn't knowingly and willfully orchestrate the deaths by cold iron. In doing so, they allowed Banality to claim part of their soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029030#post1029030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would someone repeat and implement such weaponry? Or maybe it'll be assembled and clanked loudly, but never used, like nuclear weapons? Heavily supervised (much more, than normally)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out DA: Darkening Sky. That's basically what led to the Shattering. The fae have already done irreparable damage to the two worlds and nearly ended their own existence. A repeat of a conflict on the scale of the War of Courts would probably obliterate the Dreaming once and for all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:50:55-08:00","id":1029062,"title":"","content":"Blasted! Forum ate my respons<b>^W</b> Nope, weird, it didn't. <b>UPD: </b>I re-opened this page several times, there was no my post. Weird.<br /> <br /> I was thinking, that sufficiently motivated anti-hero and Shadow Court member can do such atrocity even when fully realizing the potential consequences (including judgement and scorn of other kithains), which in turn would demand even more tragic aftermath.<br /> <br /> I mean, chimerical death provides great artistic licence in terms of what and what cannot be done within a setting, but while changeling war over Concordia were mostly bloodless (with exception for one crazy night), the result of this war was very real: an occupation of the Concordia by Sidhe. King David's actions to smooth things out are commendable, but &quot;War in Concordia&quot; proves them to be insufficient...<br /> <br /> I was always wondering, why no one, including nockers didn't use weaponry such as this, one to throw off Sidhe' conquest? To stay, commoners are here to stay. In terms of mutual hatred and friendship it would've been pretty much the same setting, except for Camarilla/Sabbath geopolitics. Commoners had the advantage of home field, knowledge and Banality (however unlikely ally, but still) on their side. Sidhe's arrogance alone may have been their undoing. Alas, it wasn't what happened.<br /> <br /> What was that? Fear? Taboo? Unwillingness to win at all costs?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-09-2017, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:58:52-08:00","id":1029068,"title":"","content":"As I said above, the Kithain have already been down that road once. The Dreaming and all fae life is hanging by a thread because of it. If that path is ever taken again, there will probably be no more Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:00:58-08:00","id":1029070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029058#post1029058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death by cold iron isn't just murder. It's the annihilation of a piece of the Dreaming. A changeling might be able to justify or rationalize it in their own mind, such as ending a Lost One or a Dauntain, but no matter the reason, it is always the destruction of a piece of the Dreaming and a victory for Banality. Just because the changeling didn't physically light the fuse, doesn't mean they didn't knowingly and willfully orchestrate the deaths by cold iron. In doing so, they allowed Banality to claim part of their soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean, that whoever ordered to provoke and anyone who helped them to execute orders to start <b><i>Night of Iron Knives </i></b>- immediately evaporated (<b>in chimerical sense </b>- Banality feedback for so many victims should be strong enough to threaten them with complete Undoing) afterwards?<br /> <br /> Or is it just your interpretation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-09-2017, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:07:40-08:00","id":1029074,"title":"","content":"The souls of the perpetrators of the Night of Iron Knives almost certainly bear the scars of their deeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:15:05-08:00","id":1029077,"title":"","content":"It's not as bad as <i>certain </i>death. They may even wear those, as sorta badges of honor.<br /> <br /> There's even whole Judgement scenario, revolving around seting up a controllable Winter with Shadow Court on the throne.<br /> <br /> Even if the other scenarios were true (some of them make Eternal Winter even less of an issue), SC certainly don't give a damn about collaterals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029058#post1029058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out DA: Darkening Sky. That's basically what led to the Shattering. The fae have already done irreparable damage to the two worlds and nearly ended their own existence. A repeat of a conflict on the scale of the War of Courts would probably obliterate the Dreaming once and for all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought DA: Fae and C:tD are completely different settings? I mean those had two different contunuities with different cosmologies and everything, weren't they? *confused*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-09-2017, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:31:10-08:00","id":1029086,"title":"","content":"DA: Fae was definitely a reference for one of my sections in C20 and another C20 project I'm working on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T09:12:30-08:00","id":1029106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029086#post1029086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DA: Fae was definitely a reference for one of my sections in C20 and another C20 project I'm working on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Grat! &lt;3 &lt;3 &lt;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T09:43:03-08:00","id":1029126,"title":"","content":"Back on topic.<br /> <br /> Because of these stated dangers, consequences and costs this crazy idea seems like a very good dramatic move for some chronicles.<br /> <br /> Though, if I were Sidhe I'd keep an eye on suspicious iron shipments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T11:09:50-08:00","id":1029162,"title":"","content":"I think there's something important missing in your whole calculus from the beginning. Forget the cold iron for a moment, you're still talking about murdering a bunch of people with a canon. That level of violence isn't the norm for Changeling society or most Changeling games in my experience. Part of what is interesting about Changeling is that is has several options for resolving violence that don't have to include lethal force, fitting when you think about the fairy tale veneer that their world has. This isn't to say that acts of shocking violence and murder can't or shouldn't happen in Changeling, but that the escalation of getting there should be meaningful and the consequences of it should be appropriately tragic and horrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T13:08:41-08:00","id":1029218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029162#post1029162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's something important missing in your whole calculus from the beginning. Forget the cold iron for a moment, you're still talking about murdering a bunch of people with a canon. That level of violence isn't the norm for Changeling society or most Changeling games in my experience. Part of what is interesting about Changeling is that is has several options for resolving violence that don't have to include lethal force, fitting when you think about the fairy tale veneer that their world has. This isn't to say that acts of shocking violence and murder can't or shouldn't happen in Changeling, but that the escalation of getting there should be meaningful and the consequences of it should be appropriately tragic and horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Imagine, that eldritch abominations, with mindnumbingly stunning looks</span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> and enchantingly </span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">sweet voices, </span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">wrapped in best</span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> garments and</span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> armed with mind raping magics, they used with ease from the times immemorial; Kings and warlords, who had sworn to protect your people and then betrayed everyone, betrayed <i><b>you</b></i> to run away, suddenly appear out of Mists six hundred years after, as if nothing had happened; Then they attack your leaders, starting a march to enslave you and your breathen into their backwards culture, to destroy all you've built and </span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">take all you had left,</span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> making you into a maid, court jester or something.<br /> <br /> Dreaming doesn't punish tortures, slavery and racism, only oathbreaking and murder. If you'd look at Sidhe's Frailties in Far Dreaming and deeper, you'll see that they are conditioned to not empathize and care about Commoners beside the word of their Oaths.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u200bIt's basically apocalyptic plot for <i><b>Changeling: the Lost! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b></i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">We know, that it isn't <i>entirely</i> correct and with a minimal effort you can spin the similar tale for nobility (it's just how war propaganda works [and everyone uses it]), but if you're a commoner and you have good reason to believe that, <i><b>what price is too high to stop such monsters?</b></i></span></span><br /> <br /> I'm not serious, just trying to immerse you to think, how far-fetched (or not) it can be sor someone to commit such an atrocity, as I suggested. There're a lot of bad blood between Nobles and commoners. And &quot;War in Concordia&quot; is a <i>thing</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-09-2017, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T13:54:21-08:00","id":1029244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea#post1028953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a war going.<br /> <br /> You hire a bunch of human gangers/mercs, give them a cannon, charged with cold iron shrapnel and ask them to fire it into the charging army of changelings. Sidhe, for example.<br /> <br /> What happens next?<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring the whole discussion on Cold Iron and the effects on the Dreaming. The situation gets on the 24 news channels because &quot;Gang uses cannon&quot; is crazy news. You get all sorts of big time government agencies checking in because &quot;that sounds like an act of terrorism&quot; and if you're in a crossover game say hello to the Men in Black.<br /> <br /> <br /> Seriously a cannon shooting cold iron scrap metal as a mass of random people even in the WOD is going to be serious on the WTF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T13:55:42-08:00","id":1029245,"title":"","content":"You're not wrong that one can easily spin Changeling into horror and you're not wrong that its easy to spin the Sidhe as monsters. You can absolutely run a game of Changeling that is about Lovecraftian guerrilla warfare. I'm down with that. What you seem to implying though is that this is a natural and inevitable outgrowth of the setting, which I don't think is true. Even beyond the setting, its a question of genre. Like I said earlier, you can totally take Changeling into a different and much more brutal genre. Human darkness lurking beneath a sugar coating is a big part of Changeling that I love. It isn't really the default genre though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T14:15:22-08:00","id":1029257,"title":"","content":"Need I remind you, that Red Caps <i>occasionaly</i> eat people? Dauntain red cap is 'evil', only because she eats changelings instead.<br /> <br /> I mean, C:tD, as presented in first and second editions is neither dark or lighthearted. It's a mash up of different subgenres and undertones, ranging from cosmic horror to childhren's journey in to magical lands. There are creatures of nightmares and hope. There is a mechanics for unseelie glamour and soul sucking magical rape and for creating puffy enchanted pony friends. Pooka pranksters, who drive banal people insane by enchanting them and power of True Love, that conquers all.<br /> <br /> I think, it's you, who ignores all the darkest parts to have a coherent over-all postitive changeling setting. (Not, that I think it's wrong)<br /> <br /> Changelings was <i>always</i> a mess and, while I am aware it is rather a flaw, than a virtue, I never ignored neither darker nor lighter aspects , unless it stood in a way of good plot. Attempts to make it into epic fantasy or gritty personal horror about loosing you mind I don't see as wrong either.<br /> <br /> Actually, <b>I'm very interested, how it would look like in C20</b>. Even DA:F is referenced, as Pooka Knight claims, which was completely different game, I thought.<br /> <br /> That said, my picture for you wasn't specifically a picture of a setting, but a picture of the wotld from inside of a specific character's mindset. I don't think you'd argue, that regardless of setting's tone, characters within setting might see it very differently. Especially, Unseelie. Wordlviews of the Shadow Court I wouldn't even address. And you can't deny, that Night of Iron Knifes actually happened. Modern changelings actually bow and swear to Sidhe feudals in exchange for 'protection' and political landscape is... tense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-09-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T14:36:18-08:00","id":1029268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029245#post1029245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said earlier, you can totally take Changeling into a different and much more brutal genre. Human darkness lurking beneath a sugar coating is a big part of Changeling that I love. It isn't really the default genre though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would <b><i>you</i></b>, modern free american person, pledge an allegiance for life to the ancient elven sorcerer, who can charm you into awe and issue offers you can't refuse? Just because you weren't born into certain kith?<br /> <br /> Or how would you feel, if you were peer-pressured into doing so, when you were <i>thirteen</i>, or say,<i> six</i>?<br /> <br /> It's Magic Mafia. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You can't simply run away, because you probably have all your mortal friends and relatives around (<i>before</i>, not afterwards - you wouldn't want to become Oathbreaker, wouldn't you?), and said mafia controls two thirds of all freeholds in a country, freeholds you <i>need</i> to survive. Smart noble even has big flaming sword and several <i>obedient</i> Troll goons, just in case he'll need to remind you your place. Then, imagine, that you're in the middle of the (Un)Seelie Mafia's domain, adding ideological tensions to your plate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-09-2017, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T14:59:44-08:00","id":1029278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029244#post1029244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously a cannon shooting cold iron scrap metal as a mass of random people even in the WOD is going to be serious on the WTF.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought the same about War of Concordance.<br /> <br /> Large scale civil disorder between two shadowy groups, each one's members are in no meaningful way connected to each other and honestly can't recall, why they were doing it. You need either magic or technocracy to cover that up.<br /> <br /> Or both <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-09-2017, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:07:25-08:00","id":1029312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029278#post1029278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought the same about War of Concordance.<br /> <br /> Large scale civil disorder between two shadowy groups, each one's members are in no meaningful way connected to each other and honestly can't recall, why they were doing it. You need either magic or technocracy to cover that up.<br /> <br /> Or both <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> 1, The war is An america thing the majority of the fighting was during a period of major protesting.<br /> <br /> 2. All the effects were chimerical or of the Dreaming thus covered up by high levels of supernatural effects.<br /> <br /> 3,. At most looks like a bunch of people getting into a fist fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which a real honest to god cannon, or more accurately a home made explosive device set off in a large crowd is not. The problem with the plan is the pure mundanity of it. Its not going to get covered by the Mists, or be completely unobserved by mortals. This will clearly be a terrorist act. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T04:11:05-08:00","id":1029544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029312#post1029312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3,. At most looks like a bunch of people getting into a fist fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think more, like couple thousands across the country at the same time. It's a full scale gang war, but with druggies.. but they don't have any drugs in their blood..<br /> <br /> Mists protect magical happenings, but if bunch of teenagers start to play a Fight Club all of a sudden and one of them drops dead (or unconscious) it will be noticed, regardless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029312#post1029312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which a real honest to god cannon, or more accurately a home made explosive device set off in a large crowd is not. The problem with the plan is the pure mundanity of it. Its not going to get covered by the Mists, or be completely unobserved by mortals. This will clearly be a terrorist act.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except when you have some useful parlor trick, like, say, <b>Chicanery 2+Prop 3 </b>to hide the cannon.<br /> <br /> Remember, you don't need to have a <i>cannon </i>out of cold iron. Just it's buckshot projectiles. With <b>Nature 5</b> you might not bother with cannon at all and cast it on sound itself.<br /> <br /> Dead bodies will be trickier, but still doable. Hm... Makes sense, how kithains hide their battles, actually. No one really needs everyone to ask questions about trust fund kid, kindergartener, TV show host and hobo shouting and fighting imaginary godzilla in the downtown. Thus, Veiled Eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-10-2017, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T11:13:42-08:00","id":1029666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029544#post1029544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think more, like couple thousands across the country at the same time. It's a full scale gang war, but with druggies.. but they don't have any drugs in their blood..<br /> <br /> Mists protect magical happenings, but if bunch of teenagers start to play a Fight Club all of a sudden and one of them drops dead (or unconscious) it will be noticed, regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between '69 and '72 that really wasn't particularly outside business as usual. Between riots, protests, mass brawls, love ins, and other upheavals the general consensus in America at the time was of society coming apart at the seems. There were people in the midwest who thought MLK was going to lead a marauding black motorcycle gang out of the Chicago slums to burn down small white towns. That's not hyperbole, that was an actual paranoid theory going around (from a few years previous obviously). The sudden boom in drug culture had provoked a moral panic in response and the man on the street really had no idea how any of them actually worked beyond a generalized hysteria. The Accordance War flying under the radar, particularly in an era with less mass communication than today, is honestly one of the more believable things about it. <br /> <br /> You are absolutely right though that if somebody dies its going to be a big deal. That's kind of what we've been saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T11:19:16-08:00","id":1029668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029544#post1029544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think more, like couple thousands across the country at the same time. It's a full scale gang war, but with druggies.. but they don't have any drugs in their blood..<br /> <br /> Mists protect magical happenings, but if bunch of teenagers start to play a Fight Club all of a sudden and one of them drops dead (or unconscious) it will be noticed, regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. There are big dust ups all the time. And you ignore this was in the middle of an solid upswing in protest culture.<br /> <br /> <br /> What you plan will look like someone set of an IED at a BLM protest. Vs There was Violence at a Protest. Both will get on the News one will be chalked up to protesters, the other will be an act of terrorism and not only get on the news but also federal investigations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except when you have some useful parlor trick, like, say, <b>Chicanery 2+Prop 3 </b>to hide the cannon.<br /> <br /> Remember, you don't need to have a <i>cannon </i>out of cold iron. Just it's buckshot projectiles. With <b>Nature 5</b> you might not bother with cannon at all and cast it on sound itself. </div> </div> </div><br /> First lets be real. Cannons don't work like that. What you are making is a IED with cold iron shrapnel.<br /> <br /> You also can't &quot;just cover the weapon but not the bullets&quot;.<br /> <br /> So we're starting at a base difficulty of 14 for the cantrip, so 5 glamour to start to get a difficulty of 9(Most you can spend), its wyrd so six glamour. for your cannon or IED. We wil assume this is planned so you get a level 5 bunk to pull this off so a difficulty of 4<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dead bodies will be trickier, but still doable. Hm... Makes sense, how kithains hide their battles, actually. No one really needs everyone to ask questions about trust fund kid, kindergartener, TV show host and hobo shouting and fighting imaginary godzilla in the downtown. Thus, Veiled Eyes. </div> </div> </div>Same math as the last one with 6 glamour, difficulty 4 to cover one body, 5 to apply the scene realm and and a glamour cost of 7.<br /> <br /> <br /> That is 13 glamour and 2 level 5 bunks thrown at this plan, and then we have the question of whether or not cold iron's innate banality eats at Cantrips, the fluff says yes, though there is no mechanical effect. As an ST I'd be tempted to just blanket say &quot;you can't use cantrips to cover Cold Iron. period&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T11:25:27-08:00","id":1029671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029544#post1029544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except when you have some useful parlor trick, like, say, Chicanery 2+Prop 3 to hide the cannon.<br /> <br /> Remember, you don't need to have a cannon out of cold iron. Just it's buckshot projectiles. With Nature 5 you might not bother with cannon at all and cast it on sound itself.<br /> <br /> Dead bodies will be trickier, but still doable. Hm... Makes sense, how kithains hide their battles, actually. No one really needs everyone to ask questions about trust fund kid, kindergartener, TV show host and hobo shouting and fighting imaginary godzilla in the downtown. Thus, Veiled Eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you hide the act itself and hide all the bodies you've still up and made a large number of people disappear at the same time. That isn't less weird or attention-getting. Even beyond that, it doesn't change the fact that you're still talking about murder by bombing, which is a next level kind of carnage that Changeling doesn't really do by default. You can do it, but it takes the game into a new and very different place. It isn't a casual act, it's a paradigm shift that you build an entire story around. <br /> <br /> You also seem to be assuming that all Changeling battles automatically end with someone dying. This isn't so. Actual death is a thing that happens, but it is generally treated with greater gravity than in a lot of the other game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T18:45:01-08:00","id":1029857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1029671#post1029671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You also seem to be assuming that all Changeling battles automatically end with someone dying. This isn't so. Actual death is a thing that happens, but it is generally treated with greater gravity than in a lot of the other game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its sort of a self correcting issue in vampire. Garou mass deaths are unlikely to be in a public place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T02:52:41-08:00","id":1029975,"title":"","content":"Depends on context. Most battles don't end with anynone's death. Most important battles and wars in general, don't end without any deaths.<br /> <br /> I agree, that in changeling mass deaths are rarely a thing, but mass oppression is the a thing. Red caps is the thing. Thallain is thing. Adhene, who kill and die permanently in Dreaming for Danu knows how long, is a thing. Unseelie vs. Seelie is a thing. Commoner vs. Nobles is the a thing. Downtain vs. Kithain is the thing (and how courteuos and unlethal do you think those are?). Cold Iron Daggers in the possession of nobility to shove into someone's back is definitely a thing. <br /> <br /> Chimerical deaths happen. Imprisonment happens. Physical deaths, albeit rarer, hapen, when someone needs to disappear permanently. A cold iron deaths also happen either as a hate crimes or political stunt also happen. Sometimes. But they are resonant. Almost everybody knows about them afterwards.<br /> <br /> What is so interesting about such an action, it's that it exactly so uproaring and unprecedented. If faerie politicians do that, what prohibits some general to make the same, albeit on different scale?<br /> <br /> There will be devastation, there will be fear, there will be anger, there will be debate, a demand for justice and demand for blood. It may force suvivors to fight even more furiously or stop war dead. <br /> <br /> It's the same thing, as war crimes, that led to establishing Geneva Conventions.<br /> Reminds of using *spoiler* in *spoiler* video game. <br /> <br /> It that happened in the sixties, kithain that left would've been so screwed when the rest of the Unseelie Houses along with Adhene returned.<br /> ________________<br /> <br /> I think your math is little bit off the mark. I don't have book on me, right now, though.<br /> <br /> If we treat cannon and it's ammunition, as the same thing, we have treat the whole thing, as a cold iron - we can't cast any cantrips on it at all, right? <br /> <br /> Easier to cast on the sound itself, while a bit unorthodox, not impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-11-2017, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T03:15:47-08:00","id":1029981,"title":"","content":"That said, I wouldn't put anything like it in uplifting epic fantasy scenario about bravery, honour, nobility and their trusty commoner sidekicks.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just wanted to point out, that because it doesn't happen every day, it doesn't mean it never happens. History of changelings proves it wrong. <br /> <br /> The magnitude of it's rarity reinforces it's impact. On both players and characters.<br /> <br /> But I can move the Goal Post (sic!) for you. <br /> <br /> Is it acceptable to use a cannon, loaded with cold iron against Fomorians and/or their servants? That kind of war is definitely win or death scenario.<br /> <br /> It may or may not happen, but for the sake of the discussion, assume it does happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-11-2017, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T11:29:38-08:00","id":1030153,"title":"","content":"Changelings are rather fragile though, and you can kill them off much like a normal human, though they do soak lethal damage, so it does take a little longer. A normal IED will likely kill any nearby Changelings without cold iron, so it is pointless overkill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:27:47-08:00","id":1030179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1030153#post1030153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings are rather fragile though, and you can kill them off much like a normal human, though they do soak lethal damage, so it does take a little longer. A normal IED will likely kill any nearby Changelings without cold iron, so it is pointless overkill.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. All the addition of cold iron does is make sure you're destroying their souls as well as their lives. Hence why the use of cold iron is generally considered pretty heinous, and doubly so on this scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:41:03-08:00","id":1030283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1030153#post1030153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings are rather fragile though, and you can kill them off much like a normal human, though they do soak lethal damage, so it does take a little longer. A normal IED will likely kill any nearby Changelings without cold iron, so it is pointless overkill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh.. Point taken!<br /> <br /> I humbly concur. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Cold Iron is for permanent solutions. </span><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\ud83d\ude08</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-11-2017, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:51:47-08:00","id":1030290,"title":"","content":"Doesn't explain, why Commoners didn't win, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T16:07:52-08:00","id":1030301,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that it is because the Sidhe who came over were probably much more powerful than the Commoners. In addition, it should be unbelievably hard to fight a creature with Appearance 7, as they are too beautiful to attack. At the very least, I would have required Commoners to make a Willpower roll, with a difficulty equal to the Appearance of the Sidhe, to attack the Sidhe each time until they have sufficient exposure to overcome the natural reluctance to destroy the beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:09:08-08:00","id":1030326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1030301#post1030301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, it should be unbelievably hard to fight a creature with Appearance 7, as they are too beautiful to attack. At the very least, I would have required Commoners to make a Willpower roll, with a difficulty equal to the Appearance of the Sidhe, to attack the Sidhe each time until they have sufficient exposure to overcome the natural reluctance to destroy the beautiful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know... Actually use their (the Sidhe's) Birthright that does pretty much the same thing, but isn't a made up system you're adding on for no reason. <br /> And not terribly many Sidhe have Appearances of 7. The average will be around 4-5. <br /> But the Birthright dif can be as high as 9 for a highly ranked angry Sidhe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T08:51:37-08:00","id":1031178,"title":"","content":"ON the cannon/IED: This is not a matter of war crimes. Its a matter of don't shit in youown back yard. This is heaping helping of shit. Banality, Human issues, Technocracy if you are crossover happy. <br /> <br /> So I Imagine IF this happened it wouldn't be driven by someone who wants to get away with it, or even cares about hiding it. They'd probably carry the bomb itself into the sitaution because they want it all to end, they want the pain to stop, they want to die with a supreme act of spite against Kithain, against the Dreaming itself. At that point they aren't going to hide anything and everyone is going to be horrified.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1030290#post1030290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't explain, why Commoners didn't win, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because it wasn't commoners vs Nobles.<br /> <br /> <br /> It was a fairly disunified groups vs a fairly unified Host. Bare in mind that a signficant amount of the fighters on the Sidhe side were Autumn Commoners either out of some romantic notion of the &quot;One true King&quot; or out of a more pragmatic &quot;the Pooka Duke here is already an asshole, if i get in good with the new guys I can have real power!&quot;. Concordia wasn't run as a democracy until the Sidhe showed up, it was run as a patch work of disunified petty fiefdoms. The constitutional Monarchy High King David and the Parlament of Dreams is MORE democratic than the previous situation not less.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:34:53-08:00","id":1031238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031178#post1031178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a fairly disunified groups vs a fairly unified Host. Bare in mind that a signficant amount of the fighters on the Sidhe side were Autumn Commoners either out of some romantic notion of the &quot;One true King&quot; or out of a more pragmatic &quot;the Pooka Duke here is already an asshole, if i get in good with the new guys I can have real power!&quot;. Concordia wasn't run as a democracy until the Sidhe showed up, it was run as a patch work of disunified petty fiefdoms. The constitutional Monarchy High King David and the Parlament of Dreams is MORE democratic than the previous situation not less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, surgical application of Sovereign and Chicanery, here and there. Maybe, you're right, mind control powers may work far better, than gunnery and explosives. Especially, if your Appearance is 3+ and have magical ability to take away freeholds from non-commoners (just remembered).<br /> <br /> Make an army of brainwashed commoners and get rid of that rebel scum!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-13-2017, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:19:29-08:00","id":1031259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031238#post1031238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, you know, surgical application of Sovereign and Chicanery, here and there. Maybe, you're right, mind control powers may work far better, than gunnery and explosives. Especially, if your Appearance is 3+ and have magical ability to take away freeholds from non-commoners (just remembered).<br /> <br /> Make an army of brainwashed commoners and get rid of that rebel scum!</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be assuming the only reason commoners would fight for the Sidhe is mind control and brainwashing, when the post you quoted explicitly laid out the opposite case. Were there commoners who were compelled to serve through a combination of Oaths and Sovereign? More likely than not. That doesn't make an army's worth though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T12:19:37-08:00","id":1031284,"title":"","content":"Null.<br /> <br /> Actually, bar that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-13-2017, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T03:47:07-08:00","id":1031523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031238#post1031238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, you know, surgical application of Sovereign and Chicanery, here and there. Maybe, you're right, mind control powers may work far better, than gunnery and explosives. Especially, if your Appearance is 3+ and have magical ability to take away freeholds from non-commoners (just remembered).<br /> <br /> Make an army of brainwashed commoners and get rid of that rebel scum!</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Concordia post David is more free and equal than it was preRessurgence. And this situation didn't happen whatsoever in other parts of the world. To the Changeling World the Return of the Sidhe was like King Arthur showed up to kick Immorten Joe out of claiming the only patch of water.. along with making other places suddenly contain water again. There's lots of good reasons for siding with the sidhe that's not insanely glamour intensive on the Sidhe's part.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T06:28:00-08:00","id":1031554,"title":"","content":"Except we don't know all that much about pre-Resurgence, other it was fiefdoms and communes struggling to survive the Glamour-scarcity and I'm not sure, where exactly are you taking information about current state of affairs. Nothing what I read implied, that Sidhe's fiefdoms are better, than motleys and communes. If you read the history of changelings in the 2nd ed. Corebook you'll notice, that changelings learned to work closely to survive, put aside their differences to larger part.<br /> <br /> The big problem with Sidhe's re-establishment is that they used Resurgence to boost their PR. They didn't brought the Glamour back. Glamour surge on Earth brought them back. Did they taught changelings to surive autumn? No. Did that make seelie and unseelie work together? No. Did they bring Glamour back? No. Did they left at the first sign of trouble? Yes. Yes, they did. <br /> <br /> What makes them think, they fit to rule? <br /> <br /> And there's what I already pointed out earlier. Making servant-lord Oaths with a ruler of questionable qualities at questionable age? Outdated government system and culture? Unregulated use of magical mind control? These are exactly the problems of current mostly Seelie mostly Noble government, Unseelie Houses (especially, aligned with Shadow Court) with their own agendas use against Sidhe. <br /> <br /> Now, again, magine medieval king or emperor, even the famous King Arthur, being given rule over modern state. It will be a disaster. Benevolent dictators are a bit less rare, than unicorns and problems they create usually far greater, than the ones they solve. And I'm not talking about the past or magical reality, where alternatives can't exist. Commoners has eyes and brains, they can add two and two.<br /> <br /> Only Scattach decided to stay. They sucked it up and survived. <br /> <br /> Now, if Sidhe goes mad or paranoid? Who will replace him? Who will judge commoner, accused of something? Who will decide the distribution of resources and favours? <br /> <br /> A privileged class, forcefully lobbying it's interests in Parliament. <br /> <br /> The problem with Sidhe is that they make mistakes and wrong judgements, like any other humans and chenglings. Majority of them are not King Arthur. They aren't forced to be morally good. Tgeir legacies and cidecies are very specific in being Blue and Orange morality, more than anything. Seelie are not any better, than Unseelie in that regard. As long, as they're hinourable, expressing their superiority complex.<br /> <br /> Moreover, and it's easily noticeable, most of the noble Houses are designed with specific failures, assosiated with nobility to increase the chances of tragedy. Trigger-happy Gwydion, who think they know everything. Insatiable Liannan (not sure, if I remrmber the name right, the ones, who need one mortal per month Rhapsodied or forced to age one year per month), Fiona, with their cravinb for forbidden love, Lian has no respect, master-slaver relationship of Aesin etc. etc. It's security risks and tragedies bound happen.<br /> <br /> On a basis of kith, Sidhe aren't any better to rule, than trolls or boggans. Yes, they are pretty and sociable, but there is reason, why movie stars and TV show hosts doesn't run our governments. <br /> <br /> What makes you think, Sidhe are better? <br /> <br /> Shouldn't they also earn their right to rule? And if proven unworthy kicked out of their shiny seats of power, like they deserve?<br /> <br /> The only upside of the Sidhe's courts is that they're more fun and exciting, than governments that actually solve problems. <br /> <br /> Again, Sidhe? Are good leaders, party makers, entertainers. They're like walking reality shows. But with more dignity and duels. But being good leader doesn't mean, you should govern or that you can gover well.<br /> <br /> And compared to xenophobic Garou and gerontocratic kindred, who both see you as a pawn or cannon fodder, Sidhe, really are not that bad. They at least make vows on their own, word of which, if not spitit, they are bound to follow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:49:54-08:00","id":1031580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031554#post1031554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except we don't know all that much about pre-Resurgence, other it was fiefdoms and communes struggling to survive the Glamour-scarcity and I'm not sure, where exactly are you taking information about current state of affairs. Nothing what I read implied, that Sidhe's fiefdoms are better, than motleys and communes. If you read the history of changelings in the 2nd ed. Corebook you'll notice, that changelings learned to work closely to survive, put aside their differences to larger part.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are also not any WORSE. There are bad Sidhe Freeholds. Therefore we should presume there were shit Commoner Freeholds. We know for a fact that Commoners just moved in, claimed titles and that was that. There weren't glorious democratic bastions of Freedom. <br /> <br /> <br /> So working from the assumptions that there were both bad freeholds AND freeholds where even if the Commoner Noble wasn't bad people still had issues. Suddenly glorious Golden people show up along with a sudden resurge of glamour. <br /> <br /> This is to say you have a sizeable portion of disastified or potentially dissatisfied Commoners sitting around. Then you have someone who shows up with the narrative of restoring the way the world used to work when glamour was free, this is before you come to the fact that Changelings are LIVING NARATIVES they are even more prone to believing in the power of stories than the reasonable rational stuff. Hell taking the reasonable rational route.. is the banal way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Suffice to say there were plenty of people who signed up for the SIdhe armies of theirown free will. Maybe in the 30 years since they've come to feel used and abused. But right then and there? They were &quot;Voting for HOpe and change&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The big problem with Sidhe's re-establishment is that they used Resurgence to boost their PR. They didn't brought the Glamour back. Glamour surge on Earth brought them back. Did they taught changelings to surive autumn? No. Did that make seelie and unseelie work together? No. Did they bring Glamour back? No. Did they left at the first sign of trouble? Yes. Yes, they did.<br /> <br /> What makes them think, they fit to rule? </div> </div> </div>None of which was readily apparent at the time of the resurgence. You're coming at the idea that Sidhe are intrinsically bad from an entirely ooc perspective. I'm trying to point out how Changelings in the late 60s early 70s might have been &quot;AT LAST THE SAVIOUR HAS RETURNED&quot;. Changelings being people can be completely fucking wrong. Even with democracy you get people who are completely unqualfiied who talk the good talk and follow people's narratives and we aren't half dream creatures who need stories to live.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And there's what I already pointed out earlier. Making servant-lord Oaths with a ruler of questionable qualities at questionable age? Outdated government system and culture? Unregulated use of magical mind control? These are exactly the problems of current mostly Seelie mostly Noble government, Unseelie Houses (especially, aligned with Shadow Court) with their own agendas use against Sidhe. </div> </div> </div>These are legitimate problems, but how outdated is their government system? Its not based on true blood ties but rather various party blocks that share some social connections. Its Authoritarian this is true but that seems to work fairly well for China. Note I am not saying that china has a better system than democracy but rather authoritarian oligarchies seem to be functioning modern government models even if they are horrible for the people there in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, again, magine medieval king or emperor, even the famous King Arthur, being given rule over modern state. It will be a disaster. Benevolent dictators are a bit less rare, than unicorns and problems they create usually far greater, than the ones they solve. And I'm not talking about the past or magical reality, where alternatives can't exist. Commoners has eyes and brains, they can add two and two. </div> </div> </div><br /> And yet they didn't. We know for a fact Presidhe the FEWER freeholds were ruled by Commoner nobles who took them from the Native AMericans. We are also talking about a magical reality where part of the universe bends over backwards to acknowledge Nobility is a thing. Its not just as if King Arthur showed up tomorrow its if he showed up tomorrow.. and the Weather changed to his moods! As if the plants grew based on his situation. This is a fact of the Dreaming. It Bends and Shapes to the fashion of the rulers of an area.<br /> <br /> This is before we get into the fact that Faerie are creatures born of living stories.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only Scattach decided to stay. They sucked it up and survived. </div> </div> </div>Other SIdhe stayed only Scattach survived.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, if Sidhe goes mad or paranoid? Who will replace him? Who will judge commoner, accused of something? Who will decide the distribution of resources and favours?<br /> <br /> A privileged class, forcefully lobbying it's interests in Parliament. </div> </div> </div>Your issue with the Sidhe is more properly an issue with Nobility. While all Sidhe have a title not all titles are Sidhe held. And while Sidhe as a Kith hold the most titles if its SIdhe vs Nonsidhe the majority of titles are held by non Sidhe even if fewer Kiths have such a higher percentage in mind.<br /> <br /> All of which you say is true about nobility in General, but it would be just as true of a Pooka or Troll, or Nocker. And there are plenty of those and they were ruling as Nobles before the Resurgence and ruling just as autocratically because the Dreaming Upholds the concept of Nobility.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem with Sidhe is that they make mistakes and wrong judgements, like any other humans and chenglings. Majority of them are not King Arthur. They aren't forced to be morally good. Tgeir legacies and cidecies are very specific in being Blue and Orange morality, more than anything. Seelie are not any better, than Unseelie in that regard. As long, as they're hinourable, expressing their superiority complex.<br /> <br /> Moreover, and it's easily noticeable, most of the noble Houses are designed with specific failures, assosiated with nobility to increase the chances of tragedy. Trigger-happy Gwydion, who think they know everything. Insatiable Liannan (not sure, if I remrmber the name right, the ones, who need one mortal per month Rhapsodied or forced to age one year per month), Fiona, with their cravinb for forbidden love, Lian has no respect, master-slaver relationship of Aesin etc. etc. It's security risks and tragedies bound happen.<br /> <br /> On a basis of kith, Sidhe aren't any better to rule, than trolls or boggans. Yes, they are pretty and sociable, but there is reason, why movie stars and TV show hosts doesn't run our governments.<br /> <br /> What makes you think, Sidhe are better? </div> </div> </div>I don't. the Dreaming seems to. As does the fact that they are the dreams of nobility given form. As for TV show hosts running governments I live in the United States of America where a completely unqualified individual won the highest office in the land without anything more than &quot;I'm famous&quot; and abuse of the power of narrative. He didn't toss around Mind control magic to get people to vote for him. And humans don't feed on glamour we just like stories.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shouldn't they also earn their right to rule? And if proven unworthy kicked out of their shiny seats of power, like they deserve? </div> </div> </div><br /> There is no fair transition of power in the Dreaming. There has never been a democratic state. The options are:Good Ruler or Revolt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only upside of the Sidhe's courts is that they're more fun and exciting, than governments that actually solve problems. </div> </div> </div><br /> They are FAIRY Governments. They shouldn't be judged on human standards. Unfortunately Changelings also have Human needs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [quote[Again, Sidhe? Are good leaders, party makers, entertainers. They're like walking reality shows. But with more dignity and duels. But being good leader doesn't mean, you should govern or that you can gover well.[./quote]<br /> <br /> <br /> If you can find me the &quot;wise vizer/senechal&quot; kith....well they probably make their way up to Vizer or Seneshal in a domain. Boggans are pretty damned good at getting that role and really who cares who wears the shiny crown when the work of running places is handled?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And compared to xenophobic Garou and gerontocratic kindred, who both see you as a pawn or cannon fodder, Sidhe, really are not that bad. They at least make vows on their own, word of which, if not spitit, they are bound to follow. </div> </div> </div>or the Heirarchy where you could litterally be a brick in the wall....<br /> <br /> Of course being Awakened is just awesome asside from the Killbots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway for a TL<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />R I am not saying the Sidhe are better rulers by human standards. I am saying Commoners had good reason to think so during the Ressurgence, enough that the Sidhe didn't need to brainwash everyone or even the majority. I am also saying the Dreaming seems to unreasonably favor both the Sidhe and Nobility in General vs more equal forms of Governance. Whether the Sidhe are good at their jobs may not matter as much when if when they cry the world rains. Its something one has to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:52:46-08:00","id":1031582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031554#post1031554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes them think, they fit to rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are reasons that touch on the structure of their society prior to the Shattering, and what came back with them in the Resurgence. Note that it's primarily what makes them *think* they're fit to rule, not necessarily what actually *makes* them fit to rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T08:14:15-08:00","id":1031590,"title":"","content":"The Garou are not that xenophobic (not more than the human societies that they associate with anyway). The Garou of Africa have joined the Ahadi and the Garou of East Asia are valued members of the Beast Courts, it is only the Western Garou, the Garou of Australia, Europe, and North America that cause major problems for others, and that is because they are infected with (or reacting against) the values of European patriarchy. Even then, the Western Garou are quite accepting of Changelings because the spirits tell them that the Changelings are doing their job better than the Western Garou are doing their job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-14-2017, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:03:46-08:00","id":1031639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031590#post1031590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, the Western Garou are quite accepting of Changelings because the spirits tell them that the Changelings are doing their job better than the Western Garou are doing their job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, probably you're right. Unless, Garou in question are Gets of Fenris and you're anyone but nunehi or troll. They'll murder you where you stand. But other, than <i>that</i>, Garou are <i>fine</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031580#post1031580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not just as if King Arthur showed up tomorrow its if he showed up tomorrow.. and the Weather changed to his moods!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking as if it's necessary a <i>good</i> thing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-14-2017, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T16:29:11-08:00","id":1031876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031639#post1031639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, probably you're right. Unless, Garou in question are Gets of Fenris and you're anyone but nunehi or troll. They'll murder you where you stand. But other, than <i>that</i>, Garou are fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Fenris's children can kinda be like that with everyone, not just changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T18:54:42-08:00","id":1031913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031590#post1031590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even then, the Western Garou are quite accepting of Changelings because the spirits tell them that the Changelings are doing their job better than the Western Garou are doing their job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really? The general feeling that the Umbra has about the Dreaming is that it's not terrible, but it's not that changelings are doing their jobs better so much as it is that anything in Werewolf has an opinion of changelings that generally falls under &quot;they're doing... something. Stay focused, and don't get too enwrapped in what the other people are doing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, I see we again run into the miscommunication between Changeling and Werewolf lore.<br /> <br /> Changeling: Some sidhe forced Fenrir to stay in Hispo for like a thousand years and now the Get all hate everyone but trolls.<br /> Get of Fenris Tribebook: What what? Oh, right, alfar. They don't matter and giants are sort of okay, next question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T21:44:42-08:00","id":1031981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031639#post1031639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're talking as if it's necessary a <i>good</i> thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>If the laws of nature bent to the Lord's move I sure as hell might reconsider &quot;Divine Right of Kings&quot; and I'm not a half fairy creature of dreams. SInce the Dreaming itself seems to uphold the whole situation there's really only one direction to go if you don't like nobles and soap opera.. just keep upping that Banality trait and it all won't matter!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T22:24:19-08:00","id":1031992,"title":"","content":"Nature, bent the Lord's whims is a huge pain in your a... head, really. Just wait for the mood swings or depressions (and with Sidhe they're guaranteed)<br /> <br /> No, that's wrong. <hr />But, there is a solution.<br /> <br /> First, dethrone Sidhe. Then kill Fomorians. Everyone. Then you should kill Banality. Right in the heart!<br /> <br /> In that order.<br /> <br /> If Technocracy, Pentex, Nephandi or Shadow Court will stand in your way, kill them too.<br /> <br /> This isn't a Changeling Way.<br /> <br /> That's <a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Old_Man_Henderson\" target=\"_blank\">Old Man Henderson</a>'s Way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-15-2017, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T22:36:26-08:00","id":1031997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031992#post1031992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nature, bent the Lord's whims is a huge pain in your a... head, really. Just wait for the mood swings or depressions (and with Sidhe they're guaranteed)<br /> <br /> No, that's wrong. <hr />But, there is a solution.<br /> <br /> First, dethrone Sidhe. Then kill Fomorians. Everyone. Then you should kill Banality. Right in the heart!<br /> <br /> In that order.<br /> <br /> If Technocracy, Pentex, Nephandi or Shadow Court will stand in your way, kill them too.<br /> <br /> This isn't a Changeling Way.<br /> <br /> That's <a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Old_Man_Henderson\" target=\"_blank\">Old Man Henderson</a>'s Way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You dethrone six sidhe through violent revolution. You kill all six of them as part of your &quot;everyone&quot; plan. You are now Undone as Banality rips your fairy soul apart. Thank you for playing. Here's your consolation prize: you are now a black hole in the Dreaming. Cheers!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T00:10:30-08:00","id":1032026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031997#post1031997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's your consolation prize: you are now a black hole in the Dreaming. Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNow, where I come from we call these things Great Maelstroms! They're good for your face.<br /> <br /> Six? Why six? I thought, there's an unspecified number of Fomorians in each Court.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T01:04:50-08:00","id":1032038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1032026#post1032026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNow, where I come from we call these things Great Maelstroms! They're good for your face.<br /> <br /> Six? Why six? I thought, there's an unspecified number of Fomorians in each Court.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Six is about how many it would take to earn the average changeling enough Banality to hit 10 dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T04:15:18-08:00","id":1032077,"title":"","content":"As much as I understand, killing others in Dreaming doesn't count against whole &quot;Oh, you can't kill them. They are but a last Vestiges of Dreaming!&quot; <br /> <br /> Adhene (and chimera) killed each other for thousands of years in Deep Dreaming. You know, how big is their Banality score? <br /> <br /> Zero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-15-2017, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T04:53:32-08:00","id":1032083,"title":"","content":"I think you kinda miss the point of Nobility being magically acknowledged by the Dreaming. It's not that sidhe believe they are of Divine Rights, they ARE of Divine Rights. The fact that they are incompetent (which is not a rule because sidhe are taught in the way of ruling) is not relevant here. Being a noble is a magical thing in the setting, even more so for sidhe (I'm not sure whether or not noble commoners warp chimerical reality in their domain the way sidhe do).<br /> Plus, when sidhe arrived, they came with lost knowledge and lost magic (btw, I wonder how commoners did with the Saining without the Naming Art in the interregnum). They came in savior. a lot of Commoners thought Spring was here again. The sad thing is sidhe did not came to save them, instead they fled something.<br /> <br /> Sidhe being dicks is not that relevant, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","user":"Nitenshi","date":". 01-15-2017, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T05:10:45-08:00","id":1032087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1032077#post1032077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I understand, killing others in Dreaming doesn't count against whole &quot;Oh, you can't kill them. They are but a last Vestiges of Dreaming!&quot; <br /> <br /> Adhene (and chimera) killed each other for thousands of years in Deep Dreaming. You know, how big is their Banality score? <br /> <br /> Zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those weren't changelings, though. Changelings are so vulnerable because they have dual souls. Other fae are free to be murderous bastards because their inherent nature is entirely glamorous. Changelings are like magnets for Banality because of their human souls. Actions that would otherwise be meaningless to other fae are thus devastating to their own fragile balance. <br /> <br /> Killing other changelings is Banal partly because you, and the Dreaming, know that changeling souls are a finite resource in the mortal world. Chimerae in the Dreaming, meanwhile, are plentiful, and when they die, they re-enter the natural cycle. The Glamour released by a dead chimerae gets transferred to something else. Most chimerae are fleeting and insubstantial anyway. They're meant to be created and die rapidly. Whereas the immortal fae soul killed forever in the mortal world, being already half severed from the Dreaming, is just destroyed. Lost forever in an increasingly Banal world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T07:38:27-08:00","id":1032121,"title":"","content":"I'm not quite sure but I'm not even sure adhene killed in the Dreaming are really died. As far as I remember, death for True Fae is just a temporary inconvenience. Their true obliteration comes in the hand of Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T08:29:29-08:00","id":1032141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1031992#post1031992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nature, bent the Lord's whims is a huge pain in your a... head, really. Just wait for the mood swings or depressions (and with Sidhe they're guaranteed)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>its not a SIdhe birthright that the Dreaming bends to their moods. Its a matter of being Noble.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lets say we decide to be fully democratic fiefdom and hold regular elections. You'll probably get a Sidhe, because people like pretty people. If not you'll get a Pooka(Second most enobled kith!) then Trolls because (they will protect us). So you have your election and because its America the Dreaming upholds the concept of a Democratic Election(unlike reality). So you now have an Elected official who serves for 4 years who runs the Fiefdom. Yay democracy.<br /> <br /> And then they get depressed and it rains.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Dreaming runs on Symbolism and fairytale logic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Its a fucked up system of watery tarts lobbing Scimitars at random people!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 01-15-2017, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T08:40:16-08:00","id":1032145,"title":"","content":"The problem is you can't reject the system of nobility entirely because whether or not <i>you</i> acknowledge or believe in nobility has no bearing at all on the fact that the Dreaming very much <i>does</i>. You could elect a leader and say that they won't be enfiefed or hold title, and then literally the first titled Changeling to come along can just take your Freehold from you and the Dreaming says &quot;Yup, that's legit.&quot; <br /> <br /> Elected monarchies are the best that most Changeling domains can manage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T09:09:14-08:00","id":1032157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1032077#post1032077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adhene (and chimera) killed each other for thousands of years in Deep Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adhene aren't Kithain. They operate on slightly different rules. Likewise, only certain chirmera warrant Banality from killing them. They're not nearly the fixed point in the Dreaming that the Kithain are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T10:52:52-08:00","id":1032207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1032145#post1032145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is you can't reject the system of nobility entirely because whether or not <i>you</i> acknowledge or believe in nobility has no bearing at all on the fact that the Dreaming very much <i>does</i>. You could elect a leader and say that they won't be enfiefed or hold title, and then literally the first titled Changeling to come along can just take your Freehold from you and the Dreaming says &quot;Yup, that's legit.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That ... really isn't the case. It may seem like that way on the surface, but in reality, the Dreaming's view on a freeholder's legitimate claim to a balefire is deeper and much more complex than that. Book of Freeholds will cover this in much more depth. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T11:08:37-08:00","id":1032220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1032207#post1032207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That ... really isn't the case. It may seem like that way on the surface, but in reality, the Dreaming's view on a freeholder's legitimate claim to a balefire is deeper and much more complex than that. Book of Freeholds will cover this in much more depth.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>Yaaaaaaa~ay!</b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:07:42-08:00","id":1032967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1032220#post1032220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Yaaaaaaa~ay!</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doesn't mean its a simple case of &quot;person with a title is just an asshat with a piece of paper either&quot; title is upheld by the Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:13:05-08:00","id":1032972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1032967#post1032967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Doesn't mean its a simple case of &amp;quot;person with a title is just an asshat with a piece of paper either&amp;quot; title is upheld by the Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said. It's complex and can be complicated by certain kinds of Treasures, Oaths and joint ownership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T00:26:48-08:00","id":1033201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nitenshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1032121#post1032121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not quite sure but I'm not even sure adhene killed in the Dreaming are really died. As far as I remember, death for True Fae is just a temporary inconvenience. Their true obliteration comes in the hand of Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed this one earlier. One of the differences between the Adhene and Kithain is that the Adhene aren't immortal. They have long lifespans compared to a human, but they still age and die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T00:56:04-08:00","id":1033213,"title":"","content":"So in case of kithain killing one is a crime against nature of Dreaming. (They're immortal and so being permanently dead is unnatural, wrong to them)<br /> <br /> In case of Adhene, killing one shouldn't be considered as such?<br /> <br /> So, what about Fomorians? <br /> <br /> My feeling is that, Thuatha and Fomorians are not creations of Dreaming, but masters (unless another side is conserned, hence War of Trees) and most rules don't apply to them, therefore, it's not as much that Dreaming will punish for killing one, as it might be (nearly) impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-17-2017, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:13:51-08:00","id":1033296,"title":"","content":"The Kithain are the successors to the Tuatha de Danaan as stewards of the Dreaming. Failure to uphold their oaths and foster the Tuathan Dream is what got them into such dire straights in the first place. For the Kithain, killing off any of the Dreaming's children is an invitation for Banality.<br /> <br /> The Fomorians haven't set foot on Earth since well before Banality became a going concern. There's no telling what would happen if a Fomorian were exposed to Banality. Their servants, however, seem to be bound to much the same rules as the Kithain \u2014 a situation that infuriates the Thallain endlessly and has some pretty disturbing implications to Kithain philosophers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:09:12-08:00","id":1033424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1033201#post1033201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I missed this one earlier. One of the differences between the Adhene and Kithain is that the Adhene aren't immortal. They have long lifespans compared to a human, but they still age and die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? Right then. I remembered something about them being reborn when they died. But I must have mix things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T17:36:54-07:00","id":1085244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1033296#post1033296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kithain are the successors to the Tuatha de Danaan as stewards of the Dreaming. Failure to uphold their oaths and foster the Tuathan Dream is what got them into such dire straights in the first place. For the Kithain, killing off any of the Dreaming's children is an invitation for Banality.<br /> <br /> The Fomorians haven't set foot on Earth since well before Banality became a going concern. There's no telling what would happen if a Fomorian were exposed to Banality. Their servants, however, seem to be bound to much the same rules as the Kithain \u2014 a situation that infuriates the Thallain endlessly and has some pretty disturbing implications to Kithain philosophers.</div> </div> </div> </div>could it be possible that the Fomorians and The Tuatha are more similar than modern fae think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T06:10:39-07:00","id":1085430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1028953-crazy-idea?p=1033296#post1033296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kithain are the successors to the Tuatha de Danaan as stewards of the Dreaming. Failure to uphold their oaths and foster the Tuathan Dream is what got them into such dire straights in the first place. For the Kithain, killing off any of the Dreaming's children is an invitation for Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they were so hamstrung by those same oaths and limitations, that there was no way to do their jobs effectively and they were bound to inevitable failure right from the beginning.<br /> <br /> If you want something done &quot;right&quot; you hire some automatons. Thuata could just let Kithain live as they were and do <i>their</i> dream on their own. Or, you know - communicate, interact, uplift. That kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> As it is, Kithain is more like convenient scapegoats, left to sort out this whole mess on their own, tasked with impossible obligations, before they even could make an informed whether they should take those oaths or not in a first place.<br /> <br /> Just like the Fallen.<br /> <br /> You will take those oaths. You will break them. You will pay. Because of course, you will. It's your Destiny.<br /> <br /> On the flipside, that's a genre convention so, of course, it's supposed to be that way and characters shouldn't question some of the things. Otherwise, the whole world will crumble apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 04-29-2017, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}